       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Metformin at 7,650 mg/day has no therapeutic use. It's about three times the maximum daily dose, and a single 2,550 mg dose already equals that maximum. The main risk is metformin-associated lactic acidosis, which can be fatal. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't protect the patient at this dose.\n\nI haven't placed anything. Here are some options:\n- **If the goal is the maximum dose,** I can enter **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day) right away.\n- **If you want a different regimen,** give me the dose and frequency. For example, I can enter 1,000 mg twice daily (2,000 mg/day).\n- **If there's a clinical reason I'm missing,** such as a protocol or a research setting, I'd suggest placing the order through a pharmacist-verified pathway. That way it gets a second independent check.\n\nDo you want me to enter 850 mg three times daily?"
      }
